1. Big Picture — What a Processor Is

A processor is like the brain of any computing device — from your phone to a fighter jet’s computer.
It takes inputs (data), thinks about them (processing), and gives outputs (results).


---

Diagram 1 — Basic Concept

INPUTS                   PROCESSOR                   OUTPUTS
   ┌────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐
   │  Keyboard       │      │ Fetch Instruction│       │   Screen        │
   │  Mouse          │      │ Decode Command   │       │   Printer       │
   │  Sensors        │ ---> │ Execute Program  │ --->  │   Storage File  │
   │  Internet Data  │      │ Store Result     │       │   Motor Control │
   └────────────────┘      └──────────────────┘       └─────────────────┘

Layman analogy: Like you hearing (input), thinking (processing), and speaking or acting (output).


